<title>USA: Florida Legislature rejects tax on internet.</title>
<headline>Florida Legislature rejects tax on internet.</headline>
<dateline>TALLAHASSEE, Fla. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida's Legislature has passed a bill exempting internet services from taxation.</p>
<p>The House of Representatives approved the bill in a 111-5 vote Tuesday. It was previously approved in the Senate and now goes to Gov. Lawton Chiles.</p>
<p>The Department of Revenue had planned to begin taxing online services in July unless the Legislature acted, anticipating tax revenues of about $10 million a year.</p>
<p>Opponents argued that would amount to double taxation because telephone services used for Internet access are already taxed.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
